Additionally, the following cannot be attempted nor interacted with during a Quasi-Realm:
* [[Triumphs]] (however, previously finished Triumphs and their relevant upgrades/rewards are available)
* Unfinished [[Challenges]]
* [[Trial of Skill]]

==Delusions==
[[File:{{#setmainimage:Delusion.png}}|thumb|x128px|right|Delusion]]
You will gain Delusions by doing well in Quasi-Realms where you will be required to hit a goal. For example, the Rainforest requires you to hit e1200 mana, and then you will gain 1 delusion, after that you get an additional delusion every +e300 mana you earn on top of the original e1200. Each Quasi-Realm has their own set of rules on this, and functions based on a high-score system - so if you replay the same Quasi-Realm you will have to beat your last high score in order to gain anything.

Earning at least 1 Delusion in a Quasi-Realm will consider it as "completed" upon switching realms and will allow you to access other Quasi-Realms that have it as a prerequisite.

Delusions are spent on [[Paramnesics]] (a subset of [[Realm Upgrades]]) which provide another form of progression.

