===Decadence===
[[File:QuasirealmsMap Decadence.png|thumb|x128px|right|Decadence Node Portrait]]
{{QuasiRealm
|description=Figuring out the deepest mysteries of the universe turned out to be easier than expected. But what purpose does that knowledge even serve?
|requirements=1.00e6 Memories
|prerequisites=None
|delusion=e1500 Mana (+e150)
|rules={{!}}
* Mysteries formula is changed, requiring e1 more Mana per e1 more Mysteries
* Mysteries earned reduce Mysteries Power e1 for every e2 Mysteries earned, proportionally
* [[Mythic Forge]] is unavailable
* Only Foundation Heritages are available
|unlocks={{SpellTooltip|Void Lure (Enhanced)}} at 5 Delusions<br><small>(''at least 1.01e2100 Total Mana, accounting for display rounding'')</small>
|guide=None - treat this as if any regular Prime Realm. 

To illustrate the rules a bit: Usually, if you have e1000 mana, this corresponds to (roughly) e500 mysts, which give you e500 profits.

In Decadence: e1000 mana gives you e1000 mysts (because decadence gives you more mysts), which give you e500 profits (because your mysts are weaker in decadence).
}}<!-- Patch v1.51.0 -->

